cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kgrel in a paper, please cite it as below."
title: "kgrel: reliability-aware dynamic ontology evolution for LLM-based knowledge-graph construction"
authors:
  - family-names: Mubarak
    given-names: Amna
    affiliation: "FAST-NUCES Karachi"
    email: "amnamubarakk111@gmail.com"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
repository-code: "https://github.com/AmnaMubarak/kgrel"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - large language models
  - hallucination detection
  - ontology evolution
  - information extraction
  - text2kgbench
abstract: >-
  kgrel is a research toolkit for quantifying, predicting, explaining, and
  controlling the reliability of LLM-generated knowledge triples before they
  enter a knowledge graph, including the open-world case where the ontology
  itself must evolve. It ships a reproducible pipeline over the
  Text2KGBench (Wikidata-TekGen) benchmark with three risk signals
  (source support, paraphrase instability, ontology novelty), a transparent
  insert / abstain / propose-schema-update gate, and the frozen N=300
  stratified sample used in the companion thesis.
